# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git checks source out with CRLF on Windows while prettier (run
# through eslint-plugin-prettier) expects LF — so `eslint` fails with hundreds of
# "Delete ␍" errors that have nothing to do with the code. It surfaced after a
# merge plus a reinstall rewrote endings across files nobody had edited: 758
# errors, zero of them real.
#
# Fixing it here rather than by setting prettier's endOfLine to "auto" keeps the
# committed bytes identical whoever commits them, which is what stops the next
# person seeing a diff of the whole file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
